# Publication programme — P1–P5 terminal dashboard

The repository paper terminal is `PEER_REVIEW_READY`, meaning ready for serious external review on the paper's **actual bounded claim**, not journal acceptance and not completion of every possible future expansion.

## Paper-terminal dashboard — 4 / 5
- [x] #98 — **P1 = `PEER_REVIEW_READY`** on the bounded credential-free mechanical mutation-necessity claim; broader model/open-ended superiority excluded;
- [x] #99 — **P2 = `PEER_REVIEW_READY`** on the narrowed methods / critical-system-design claim; matched external superiority remains `CANNOT_CHECK`/future work;
- [x] #100 — **P3 = `PEER_REVIEW_READY`** on the scoped P3.C5/P3.C9 already-structured public-reference mapping claim; retired raw-text/downstream atlas not fabricated;
- [x] #101 — **P4 = `PEER_REVIEW_READY`** on protected V2; #281 follow-up is non-blocking `CANNOT_CHECK`;
- [ ] #102 — **P5 Self-ORION** remains open.

**Programme terminal: 4 / 5 papers ready.**

## Shared gate reconciliation
For P1–P4, the paper-level parents now carry the authoritative claim/evidence/literature/reproduction boundaries. Shared programme services remain independent where they also cover P5 or later research:
- #160 common P1–P5 journal-package tracker remains open because not every P1–P5 package is final;
- #283 programme verification remains open for its stronger global/fresh-host objectives even though current promoted positives have receipts;
- #284 revival remains open for P5/global research; P1/P2/P3/P4 child terminals are reconciled;
- #315 recursive closure remains open at programme scope; P1/P2/P3/P4 paper-local fixed points are reconciled;
- #318 mechanism-assimilation process remains open at shared-process scope; P1/P2 paper consumer tranches are complete;
- #324 known discrepancy lane is closed `DISCREPANCIES_RESOLVED`.

## Integrity boundary
- [x] no unrun P2 external-superiority study was called positive;
- [x] no unrun P3 eight-family/raw-text study was called complete;
- [x] no unrun P4 protected-acquisition follow-up was called positive;
- [x] null/harmful/`CANNOT_CHECK` histories remain visible;
- [x] narrower supported publication tracks are allowed to close without waiting indefinitely for a maximal claim.

## Master terminal
This issue remains **OPEN only because P5 #102 is not yet `PEER_REVIEW_READY`**. P1/P2/P3/P4 are no longer open paper-readiness debt.

## Parent
Master publication programme: #97

Canonical plan: `papers/paper-05-self-orion/JOURNAL_READINESS.md`

Existing execution dependencies:
- #8 — frozen live-provider research trial;
- #76 — Phase-2 Shadow Self-ORION closure.

These are necessary evidence inputs, but they do **not** replace the paper-level nearest-work, baseline, ablation, statistics, plots and manuscript gates here.

## Goal
Bring **ORION-P5 — Self-ORION** to `PEER_REVIEW_READY` by prospectively testing whether its governed composition produces **more transferable and less compromise-prone improvement** than current self-edit/self-evolution/failure-learning baselines on hidden-cause development tasks.

## Progress snapshot — reconciled 2026-08-17

**Checklist count:** 74 / 140 items checked (~53%). The diagnostic attribution is **21/24** from raw JSONL; stale perfect-score prose is refused. Merged PR #327 / commit `b6c07d73217d708842b9bd9003658cfd1d027e2a` also adds the required P5-1 governed-development-loop figure, so that previously stale box is now checked.  
**Interpretation:** literature/design/protocol/integrity work is substantially advanced; the empirical study, protected execution, campaign results, final manuscript and journal package remain open. A checked design item does **not** convert `CANNOT_CHECK` into empirical PASS.

Merged milestones already represented below include the prospective P5 V1 protocol, nearest-work closure, staged-acceptance V2 design, fail-closed V2 run/evidence binding, P5-1, and P5-T1. Exact subject/split/provider/evaluator execution identities and external outcomes are still unbound.

## Current state — already complete
