  **persistent issue + evidence-bound causal discrimination + invention readiness + replay AND independent fresh transfer + protected evaluator/assurance + immutable negative evolution history + no self-certification/merge authority**.

## Step 2 — freeze hypotheses
Recommended primary:

**H1 — transferable improvement:** under hidden-cause development tasks, full Self-ORION produces greater protected improvement on independent fresh tasks and lower harmful-transfer rate than matched self-edit/self-evolution baselines.

Secondary:
- **H2:** competing causes + frozen discriminator reduce false method changes versus reflection/candidate-centric optimization;
- **H3:** protected assurance prevents evaluator/holdout/negative-history manipulation from being counted as improvement;
- **H4:** transfer/integrity benefit remains useful after added cost/conservatism.

- [x] freeze H1 unless preregistered pilot justifies another primary;
- [x] freeze minimum useful fresh-transfer gain / harmful-transfer margin;
- [ ] freeze evaluator custody, splits, budgets, statistical plan and plots before final outcomes. *(policy is frozen; exact execution identities remain unbound)*

## Step 2b — staged-acceptance V2 after PACE audit
