## Track question
How should the total cost of creating and using task-relevant state be measured so that preprocessing/compilation, memory, model capacity, reasoning/search, tools and verification are compared on one auditable boundary?

## Core object
For raw state `R`, target responsibility `Y`, compiler family `C`, downstream family `V`, and quality `q`, estimate a Pareto frontier rather than a single arbitrary scalar:

`W(R -> Y; V,q) = ParetoMin[ compile + state + model + inference/search + tools + verification ]`.

## Mandatory resource axes
- compiler/preprocessing operations and wall time;
- representation/state size and memory traffic;
- model parameters / interaction degree / active capacity;
- generated tokens / recurrent steps;
- search nodes / verifier calls / tool calls;
- cache/reuse cost;
- latency and energy where reproducibly measurable.

