# B. ORION-generated exact data remains mandatory

Public datasets do not cover the most important ORION coordinates cleanly. Build D0 exact families where gold comes from the generator/simulator, not an LLM.

Minimum generated families:

1. unseen mechanic composition;
2. precondition/effect structural near-miss;
3. preservation/invariant violation;
4. explicit template + role/entity binding;
5. entity-count/graph-size extrapolation;
6. symmetric unresolved binding / structural non-identifiability;
7. local pairwise consistency but global-cycle inconsistency;
8. genuinely higher-order interaction invisible to pairwise projection;
9. stale/incompatible negative history;
10. relevant defeater vs irrelevant high uncertainty;
11. observational equivalence but interventional difference;
12. sparse mechanism shift;
13. predictive shortcut broken by intervention;
14. representation failure vs mechanism failure;
15. verification unavailable / `CANNOT_CHECK` distinct from logical UNKNOWN;
16. action succeeds but irrelevant to goal / resource waste;
17. same mechanic, reminted surface/entity identities;
18. same surface, different hidden mechanic contract.

For every generated example where possible, create a **minimal counterfactual sibling** changing exactly one causally/structurally relevant coordinate.

