# C. Frozen task suite

Do not create one generic score. Each task below should have separate train/dev/protected-test results and resource accounting.

## T0 — State reconstruction
Input: admitted observation/view. Output: typed explicit state fields.
Question: can the representation recover task-relevant state without semantic leakage?

## T1 — Candidate mechanic/operator ranking
`score(S_t, candidate) -> real`
Candidate-relative; remint identities; no global mechanic-ID vocabulary.

## T2 — Applicability/precondition prediction
Predict `APPLICABLE / INAPPLICABLE / UNKNOWN` plus missing/violated precondition where exact.

## T3 — Effect / next-state prediction
`(S_t, action) -> Delta(S)` or next-state fields.
Compare final-state supervision vs transition/intermediate supervision.

## T4 — Preservation/invariant prediction
Predict which state coordinates must remain invariant after an action and detect preservation violations.

## T5 — Typed failure prediction
At minimum separate wrong binding, failed precondition, contradictory effect, stale history, impossible action, verifier/tool failure, resource exhaustion and unresolved/non-identifiable cases where the source permits exact labels.

## T6 — Template/binding generalization
Train mechanic templates with one set of entity names/roles; test reminted entities, role permutations, unseen combinations and ambiguity.

## T7 — Unseen composition
Train on atoms/short compositions; test held-out compounds, longer horizons and new combination structures (SCAN/CLRS/generated worlds).

## T8 — Inquiry / experiment selection
Given unresolved alternatives, choose the next observation/action maximizing task-relevant discrimination under a cost budget. Start in exact synthetic worlds, then ScienceWorld.

## T9 — Abstention/non-identifiability
Distinguish:
- logical UNKNOWN;
- probabilistic uncertainty;
- structural non-identifiability;
- external authority `CANNOT_CHECK`.
Score calibration and selective accuracy, not only raw accuracy.

## T10 — Evidence/receipt-conditioned state update
Given proposal + authoritative receipt, update only justified coordinates. Include hostile receipts/irrelevant evidence and ensure the learned model cannot self-authorize verification.

## T11 — Adaptive compute / stop decision
At each state decide `STOP` vs which operation/tool/mechanic to invoke. Measure success vs number of state transitions/tool calls/CPU time.

## T12 — Continual mechanic acquisition
Sequential stream:
- encounter new transition pattern;
- propose candidate mechanic;
- accumulate supporting/counterexample receipts;
- promote/split/retire mechanic under frozen rule;
- test transfer to future worlds.

Start with external memory/library updates; do not require weight updates. Later compare tiny online learner if justified.

## T13 — Language rendering/parsing layer
Keep reasoning substrate fixed; vary surface realization. Measure how much error belongs to language parsing/rendering vs state computation. Frozen pretrained LLM/API may be used only as a non-authoritative parser/proposer arm with exact downstream verification.

