# D. Baseline ladder — CPU first

For each task, start with the simplest adequate competitors:

1. deterministic oracle / exact solver where available;
2. majority/prior/random and leakage sentinels;
3. bag/count/equality feature linear/logistic model;
4. linear SVM;
5. decision tree;
6. random forest / gradient boosting;
7. kNN/case-based retrieval;
8. shallow MLP only if a nonlinear residual survives;
9. tiny sequence model (small GRU/Transformer/SSM only where feasible on CPU) as the token-sequence comparator;
10. explicit-state + same-capacity controller;
11. search/planner/probabilistic solver when that is the appropriate donor.

A frozen hosted/pretrained LLM may be evaluated zero/few-shot as an external comparator/proposal generator, but **do not fine-tune it and do not let it generate gold** in the first programme.

