# I. Success metrics / claim terminals

Do not use one headline score. Each possible claim has its own terminal.

### Reasoning
`OOD_COMPOSITION_ADVANTAGE` only if explicit-state system beats the strongest information/capacity-matched simpler/token baseline on frozen OOD axes.

### Token dependence
`LESS_SERIALIZED_REASONING` only if equal-or-better task success uses materially fewer serialized intermediate tokens/bytes; report state-size overhead too.

### Inference efficiency
`ADAPTIVE_COMPUTE_ADVANTAGE` only if equal-or-better success reduces wall CPU/operations/tool calls under matched environment and caching policy.

### Training/sample cost
`SAMPLE_EFFICIENCY_ADVANTAGE` only if learning curves show fewer examples and/or lower measured training compute to a frozen capability threshold. Count preprocessing/verifier cost separately.

### Reliability
`EPISTEMIC_RELIABILITY_ADVANTAGE` only if false-positive/false-verification behavior, abstention/non-identifiability or typed failure localization improves beyond accuracy alone.

### Continual learning
`VERIFIED_CONTINUAL_TRANSFER` only if new verified episodes/mechanics improve future tasks without unacceptable forgetting or false mechanic promotion.

Other valid terminals:
- `PUBLIC_DATA_INSUFFICIENT`;
- `STRUCTURE_GAIN_EXPLAINED_BY_SUPERVISION`;
- `STRUCTURE_GAIN_EXPLAINED_BY_EXTRA_INFORMATION`;
- `TOKEN_BASELINE_SUFFICIENT`;
- `CLASSICAL_BASELINE_SUFFICIENT`;
- `CONTAMINATION_BLOCKED`;
- `NO_INCREMENTAL_VALUE`;
- `CANNOT_CHECK`.

